---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base>
  <div class="page">
    <h1>Colophon</h1>

    <div class="section">
      <h2 class="section-label">stack</h2>
      <ul class="stack-list">
        <li>Astro static site generation</li>
        <li>TypeScript with a small content model</li>
        <li>Hand-authored CSS tokens and progressive enhancement</li>
        <li>IBM Plex Sans and IBM Plex Mono, self-hosted</li>
        <li>Vanilla custom elements for the figure and interactive affordances</li>
        <li>Static hosting with a committed content snapshot fallback</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
      <h2 class="section-label">figure</h2>
      <p>
        The signal figure is a simulation of a sensor signal with noise filtering. It uses a pure TypeScript model that drives both the animated canvas and the static SVG fallback. The readout shows the signal-to-noise ratio (SNR) in dB, computed from the same model that draws the lines.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
      <h2 class="section-label">source</h2>
      <p>
        The source code is available on <a href="https://github.com/0xASR-dev" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <style>
    .section {
      margin: var(--space-8) 0;
    }

    .section-label {
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: var(--step--1);
      color: var(--ink-muted);
      margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
    }

    .stack-list {
      list-style-type: none;
      padding: 0;
      margin: var(--space-3) 0 0;
    }

    .stack-list li {
      margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
    }

    a {
      color: var(--ink-muted);
      text-decoration: none;
      transition: color var(--dur-fast) ease-out;
    }

    a:hover {
      color: var(--accent);
    }
  </style>
</Base>